        whyItMatters:
          "The 'imprint of personality' standard, while modestly demanding in theory, is applied in practice with real flexibility by French courts, so the harder question in nearly every real French copyright dispute is not whether the bar for originality was cleared but where the free-flowing idea actually ends and the protected concrete form begins, exactly the same filtering discipline required under the US and German frameworks, arrived at through a distinctly French doctrinal vocabulary you should use correctly rather than translating back into US terms when writing or arguing in a French context.",
