        whyItMatters:
          "Spain's Article 8 framework usefully makes explicit a distinction other systems leave more implicit: a marca notoria, known within a specific relevant sector, gets somewhat narrower protection than a marca renombrada, known to the general public across sectors, which means correctly characterizing which of the two categories a given mark actually falls into materially affects how far its protection against unrelated uses actually reaches. As in Germany and France, no single confusion factor controls on its own; strong distinctiveness in the earlier mark can offset weaker similarity elsewhere in the analysis.",
        example:
          "Two moderately similar marks for closely related goods sold through overlapping channels are analyzed under the full interdependence test of Article 6, with no factor controlling alone. A mark renowned broadly among Spanish consumers generally, a marca renombrada, can invoke Article 8 against an unrelated free-riding use in a completely different market, a reach a merely sector-known marca notoria would not have outside its own specific sector.",
